# Build output
**/bin/
**/obj/

# The published app. Deliberately not versioned: it is ~360 MB of .NET runtime, and
# it is also where captured parameter files land at runtime. See the note in
# README.md about presets living inside the publish folder.
/dist/

# Saved camera credentials are encrypted per Windows account and never belong in a
# repository, wherever they end up.
*.credentials
credentials.dat

# Editor / OS noise
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Preset / parameter files. These are captured camera configurations rather than
# source: they hold site-specific settings, and a full capture carries credential
# fields (gb28181.sip_passwd, email and FTP passwords). They stay on disk so the
# build still ships them - the csproj copies presets\*.json to the output - but they
# are deliberately not versioned.
**/presets/

# Installer output. Rebuild it with installeruild-installer.cmd.
/build/
